Introspection (Noun): Apne aap ke ander jhankana.
  - He spent some time in introspection.
Gloat (Verb): Kisi ki haar ya takleef par khushi manana, doosron ko neecha dikhakar khushi feel karna.
  - He is gloating. 
Imminent (Adjective): Aane wala - coming or likely to happen very soon.
  - The US Embassy in Saudi Arabia is on alert due to an imminent threat of missile or drone attack.\
Spitfire: Tez-taraar - A person with a fiery temper who speaks quickly and angrily.
  - She is a real spitfire - never afraid to speak her mind.
Vulnerability (Noun): Atisamvedansheel, The quality of being vulnerable or something that is vulnerable.
  - India has witnessed a vulnerability in terms of its crude reserves, following the breakout of the Middle East crisis.
Outfox (Verb): Chalakhi se hara dena, To get an advantage over someone by acting more cleaverly than them.
  - India outfoxed england with clever last 3 overs plan.
  - Bharat ne aakhri 3 overon mein eak chalakh plan se england ko hara diya.
Scepticism (Noun): an attitude that shows you doubt whether something is true or useful:
  - Congress leader Sachin Pilot expressed scepticism regarding bihar CM Nitish Kumar's decision to contest for the Rajya Sabha.
  - Congress neta sachin pilot ne bihar ke mukhyamantri nitish kumar ke rajya sabha chunav ladhne ke fainsle per avishvaas jataya.
